The purpose of the current research was to determine
whether samples of beeswax taken at various ages may
include substantial differences in the values of heavy metal
concentrations. Beeswax taken from Egypt’s Behaira governorate was tested for nine heavy metals. According to
the study, new beeswax combs only contain fewer amounts
of heavy metals. The highest metal concentrations were

